{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120550","id":3912089340,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7pLb78","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120550","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120550.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120550.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120550","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120550/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120550/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120550/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/12fbe8e3f2cb753105b3341d62a40990f467dcd1","number":120550,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Fix `HTTPRequest.has_header` match logic","user":{"login":"NoNormalDev","id":190293561,"node_id":"U_kgDOC1emOQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190293561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev","html_url":"https://github.com/NoNormalDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nFixes the private function `HTTPRequest::has_header()`.\r\n\r\nThe current implementation is wrong, because it checks if the line starts with the header, when it instead should check if it matches with the entire text before \":\" :\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/d569fcf207aea355ea9d0822255ad490945f5572/scene/main/http_request.cpp#L81-L87\r\n\r\nSo, if the line is for example \"Content-Length: 123\", then `has_header(list, \"Content\")` will return `true`, when it should return `false`.\r\n\r\nI simply copied the code from the function below `get_header_value`, which is implemented correctly:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/d569fcf207aea355ea9d0822255ad490945f5572/scene/main/http_request.cpp#L95-L104\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nI also made some cleanups:\r\n\r\n- Fixed a typo (\"lowwer_case_header_name\" --> \"lower_case_header_name\")\r\n- Return early instead of keeping track of an additional variable\r\n- Change the `for (int i = 0; i < p_headers.size(); i++)` loop to a `for (const String &header : p_headers)` loop (suggested by AThousandShips)\r\n\r\nI also applied this to the neighboring function `get_header_value`, because the change is too small to put in a separate PR, and as mentioned earlier, the code is almost identical. If that's not OK, I can revert it, but I think that it makes the code cleaner and more bug-proof (`has_header` used a messy break statement `&& !exists` instead of `break;`, which is easy to miss)\r\n\r\nThis is not a breaking change, as this function is not exposed.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":649800701,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw2NDk4MDA3MDE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:network","name":"topic:network","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":nul